[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_kmn0e")
fish_name = "Sasha Splash"
grade = 3
sprite = ExtResource("2_h2nc2")
catch_blurb = "Oh my gosh, is that...really her?!"
description = "Sasha Splash (the person) was known for her bubbly FishTalk performance, where she would lip-sync a conversation between two fish in an exaggerated scenario. She also innovated the concept of interpretive fish ballet, where a terrestrial organism such as herself attempts to capture the graceful motions of aquatic life. A well-known segment of her live shows was “Swim with the Fishes,” where she educated the audience on different species of fish. 

Sasha Splash drowned during her first-ever full-submersion performance. During the distribution of assets following her untimely death, Sasha Splash (the fish) could be found abundantly in each of the star’s estates. Her in-laws involved biologists in the process to identify the species, but soon realized it was entirely undocumented. It is debated whether Sasha Splash (the person) simply discovered this species alongside her “Swim with the Fishes” team, or if she employed specialized breeding practices.

Her in-laws decided to release the species into the wild, where their bright, glittery forms stick out from the dull backdrop of aquatic sediment and vegetation. Should you catch one, try not to be discouraged by its bombastic side-eye, or distracted by its eye-catching appearance.

Interestingly, Sasha Splash (the fish) is the only officially recognized species that does not have a scientific name. This is exclusively due to licensing rights.

“Bubble your troubles, take your troubles to the trash, and splash around the dance floor!” —Sasha Splash (the person)
"
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://cr3nmjdvpgh0a"
